> we can either make the parser aware of the special characteristics of `<style>` & `<script>` tags and prohibit providing anything other than 0 or 1 VText nodes to these tags

That would cause the following to be rejected:
```rust
let one = "html { background: black  }"
let two = "body { color: while  }"

let html = html! {
    <style>
        {one}
        {two}
    </style>
};
```

> we can leave the semantics of these elements as they are and just pass the current inner-most VTag's name to `render_into_stream` functions as context, so that this context can be used in `VText::render_into_stream` to choose between `encode_text`, `encode_style` & `encode_script` functions of the `html_escape` module.

I suggest the using this approach. @schvv31n, would you like to implement it and PR? Happy to have a look at one
